# Panel skeletons & progressive loading

Prefer **layout-shaped skeletons** over a centered “Loading page…” spinner in role panels.

## Kit

| Piece | Import |
|-------|--------|
| Primitives | `@/components/loaders/skeletons` → `SkeletonPageHeader`, `SkeletonTable`, `SkeletonCalendar`, … |
| Page templates | `@/components/loaders/skeletons` → `PanelListPageSkeleton`, `PanelDetailPageSkeleton`, `PanelCalendarPageSkeleton`, `PanelDashboardPageSkeleton`, `PanelCardsPageSkeleton`, `PanelFormPageSkeleton` |

Docs: `docs/[12] Pages/skeleton-loading-plan.md` · checklist: `docs/[12] Pages/pages.md`

## Route `loading.tsx`

- Panel segments: return a **page template** that matches the route (list / detail / calendar / dashboard / form / cards).
- Always keep `TopLoaderPendingBridge` (templates already include it).
- Auth / root may keep `RouteLoading variant="full-page"` until a public skeleton exists.
- Do not put business logic or data fetching in `loading.tsx`.

```tsx
import { PanelListPageSkeleton } from "@/components/loaders/skeletons";

export default function Loading() {
  return <PanelListPageSkeleton />;
}
```

## Progressive sections

- After the route skeleton: stream heavy parts with `<Suspense fallback={primitive or small template}>`.
- Shell (title / cheap chrome) can paint first; tables, calendars, and charts wait in their own boundaries.
- Dialog-only datasets load on open — not on first paint.

## Do not

- Use `PanelRouteLoading` / center `PageSpinner` for new panel route fallbacks.
- Build a fully custom skeleton per page when a shared template fits — extend primitives instead.
- Drop the global top bar or mount a second top loader inside the panel.
- Replace submit `InlineSpinner` with page skeletons.
